# NOTE: this file is written and must be read via nitransforms
# (nitransforms.linear.load(path, fmt='fs').matrix), not FreeSurfer's own LTA
# tools -- nitransforms stores LTAs using FreeSurfer's "points convention",
# so the raw matrix numbers above are NOT the intended physical transform
# directly; only round-tripping through nitransforms' reader/writer gives
# back the correct matrix.
# Maps HiP-CT brain native physical space (mm, corner-origin: voxel (0,0,0) ->
# RAS (0,0,0), any pyramid level) to the physical RAS space of the raw
# FastSurfer segmentation output, still on FreeSurfer's own internal 320^3
# conform grid (LIA-handed storage order), supplied by a colleague alongside
# the real T1 input file.
# CREATED 2026-09-04: Matrix = (raw FastSurfer segmentation output)'s affine @
# inv(raw native sample volume's affine). Both real headers, no data-identity
# check needed (see hipct_native_to_fastsurfer_input.lta for that reasoning).
# det(3x3) = -1.0001 -- a clean signed axis permutation WITH a reflection
# (unlike hipct_native_to_fastsurfer_input.lta's det=+1), consistent with
# FreeSurfer's internal conform grid being left-handed (LIA) vs RAS's
# right-handed convention. The ~0.004% deviation from exactly +/-1 is just
# that file's header being rounded to 4 decimal places (0.4941 instead of
# 0.49408), not a real rotation component.
# Provenance (confirmed by the user + verified numerically): raw FastSurfer
# output (this file's dst space, 320^3, 96 labels) -> resampled onto the T1
# input file's grid (identical rotation to that file, zero interpolation
# needed for the reorientation itself) -> padded into a larger canvas,
# offset by an exact integer voxel shift of (4, 18, 20), to produce
# sub-01_ses-01_sample-brain_seg-freesurfer_res-494um_desc-FastSurfer_dseg.nii.gz
# (same 96-label set, confirming the lineage). So dseg's own native-space
# transform is identical to hipct_native_to_fastsurfer_input.lta's, just
# evaluated on a canvas offset by that known (4,18,20) voxel pad -- no
# separate dseg-specific transform file is needed.
